WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.467
Welcome to Micro-Transformer.

2
00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:05.936
These three showcases let you try small, real models doing different jobs.

3
00:00:05.936 --> 00:00:10.778
Start with a result, then explore what the model learned and how it

4
00:00:10.778 --> 00:00:11.150
works.

5
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:16.807
In Ava's world, a trained model chooses how she moves towards the lamp.

6
00:00:16.807 --> 00:00:19.893
You can change the room and watch what happens.

7
00:00:19.893 --> 00:00:24.350
This recorded journey succeeds, but a different challenge can still leave her stuck.

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.507
The Chatbot follows facts in short stories and generates an answer.

9
00:00:33.507 --> 00:00:36.047
It uses Micro-Transformer's small, fixed language.

10
00:00:36.047 --> 00:00:41.550
Try the examples, change a detail, and see whether the model keeps track.

11
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:47.686
Device messaging separates where an asset actually is from what its receiving hub

12
00:00:47.686 --> 00:00:48.825
has been told.

13
00:00:48.825 --> 00:00:51.863
Withhold an update and inspect the model's report.

14
00:00:51.863 --> 00:00:54.900
The devices are simulated; the prediction is real.

15
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.654
Training lets you change the practice.

16
00:00:58.654 --> 00:01:01.634
Editing examples alone doesn't teach the model.

17
00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:07.168
Click Train to update its learned weights, then return to Playground to test

18
00:01:07.168 --> 00:01:08.019
the result.

19
00:01:08.019 --> 00:01:11.850
Extra practice can help some answers and hurt others.

20
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.103
Model is the optional look under the hood.

21
00:01:16.103 --> 00:01:18.774
Inspect the structure that produces the predictions.

22
00:01:18.774 --> 00:01:21.445
Its architecture is read-only in this release.

23
00:01:21.445 --> 00:01:26.405
Each showcase keeps its own learned version, and everything you try here runs

24
00:01:26.405 --> 00:01:27.550
on your device.
